-- title:
--   Coefficients of U_ℓ on differentials: aₙ↦ a_{ℓ n}
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field, $N\ge 1$ an integer with $(N:K)\neq 0$, and $\ell$ a prime dividing $N$; let $\zeta\in K^{\times}$ be a primitive $\ell$-th root of unity. Inside $K((q))$ let $F=\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,K\,N$ be the $K$-subfield generated by $j(q)=q^{-1}\cdot j_{\mathrm{num}}$ and $j(q^{N})$, and let $R=\mathrm{charLDegeneracyRoof}\,K\,N\,\ell$ be the $K$-subfield generated by $j(q)$, $j(q^{N})$, $j(q^{\ell})$ and $j(q^{N\ell})$ (each $j(q^{M})$ being the image of $j(q)$ under the substitution $q\mapsto q^{M}$). Write $\alpha=\mathrm{heckeAlphaC}\,K\,N\,\ell$ for the inclusion $F\subseteq R$ and $\beta=\mathrm{heckeBetaC}\,K\,N\,\ell$ for the $K$-algebra map $F\to R$ given by $q\mapsto q^{\ell}$, and regard $R$ as an $F$-algebra through $\beta$, so that $K\to F\to R$ is a tower. For $\omega\in\Omega_{F/K}$ and $n\in\mathbb{Z}$ the assertion is that the $n$-th coefficient of the $q$-expansion of $\mathrm{traceDiff}\,(\alpha^{*}\omega)$ equals the $\ell n$-th coefficient of the $q$-expansion of $\omega$. Here $\alpha^{*}$ is the map $\Omega_{F/K}\to\Omega_{R/K}$ induced by $\alpha$, $\mathrm{traceDiff}$ is the $F$-linear map $\Omega_{R/K}\to\Omega_{F/K}$ chosen to satisfy $t(y\cdot\beta^{*}\eta)=\mathrm{Tr}_{R/F}(y)\cdot\eta$ (and $0$ if no such map exists), and the $q$-expansion is the $K$-linear map $\Omega_{F/K}\to K((q))$ chosen, along the inclusion $F\subseteq K((q))$, to satisfy $dx\mapsto q\,dx/dq$ and $f\omega\mapsto f\cdot$(expansion of $\omega$).
--
--   This is the classical formula $a_n(U_\ell\,\omega)=a_{\ell n}(\omega)$ in weight two for the Hecke operator $U_\ell$ at a prime $\ell$ dividing the level, realised as the trace along one degeneracy map of the pullback along the other on Kähler differentials of the function field of $X_0(N)$ over an arbitrary field in which $N$ is invertible. It is used in the verification that suitable pullbacks of differentials lie in the torsion subspaces attached to the Hecke action in characteristic $\ell$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_coeff_qExpansionDiffAlong_traceDiff_pullbackDiff_heckeAlphaC_of_dvd.lean

